.TH FBSCREENSIZE 1 "2026-09-10" "flux-tools 2.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
fbscreensize \- change screen resolution and reinitialize compositor
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B fbscreensize
.I mode
.RB [ \-n ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B fbscreensize
changes the screen resolution using xrandr and reinitializes an existing Compton on the current display, preserving its command-line options and configuration.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.I mode
Screen resolution mode (e.g., 1920x1080)
.TP
.B \-n
Skip compositor reinitialization
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR xrandr (1),
.BR compton (1)
.SH AUTHOR
Tomas-M <https://github.com/Tomas-M>
crims0n <crims0n@minios.dev>
.SH NOTES
The primary connected output is preferred, with the first connected output as fallback. Errors from xrandr are returned without touching the compositor. After success, only Compton on the current display is reinitialized with SIGUSR1, preserving its settings.
